1
00:00:12,140 --> 00:00:17,810
Love is a song that never ends

2
00:00:17,890 --> 00:00:23,690
Life may be swift and fleeting

3
00:00:23,770 --> 00:00:29,200
Hope may die
Yet love's beautiful music

4
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:34,910
Comes each day like the dawn

5
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:40,500
Love is a song that never ends

6
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:46,340
One simple theme repeating

7
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:52,090
Like the voice of a heavenly choir

8
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:58,770
Love's sweet music flows on

9
00:01:06,110 --> 00:01:11,650
Like the voice of a heavenly choir

10
00:01:12,490 --> 00:02:55,130
Love's sweet music flows on

11
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:50,100
Wake up.

12
00:04:52,170 --> 00:04:54,540
-What now?
-Wake up, Friend Owl.

13
00:04:54,630 --> 00:04:56,800
What's going on around here?

14
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:59,210
-Wake up.
-It's happened.

15
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:01,260
The new prince is born.

16
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:04,850
-We're going to see him.
-Come on. You better hurry up.

17
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:19,780
Well, look.

18
00:05:21,990 --> 00:05:24,620
-Well.
-Isn't he cute?

19
00:05:28,410 --> 00:05:32,040
Well, this is quite an occasion.

20
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:36,960
Yes, sir,
it isn't every day a prince is born.

21
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:40,800
You're to be congratulated.

22
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:44,680
-Yes, congratulations.
-Congratulations.

23
00:05:45,140 --> 00:05:46,930
Thank you very much.

24
00:05:47,390 --> 00:05:51,100
Come on. Wake up. We have company.

25
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:58,650
Hello. Hello, there.

26
00:05:58,730 --> 00:06:01,900
-Hello, little prince.
-Hello. Hello, there.

27
00:06:01,990 --> 00:06:03,740
Hello, little prince.

28
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:25,510
Look. He's trying to get up.

29
00:06:48,450 --> 00:06:50,620
Kinda wobbly, isn't he?

30
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:52,160
Thumper.

31
00:06:53,870 --> 00:06:55,870
Well, he is.

32
00:06:57,630 --> 00:06:59,290
Aren't you?

33
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:10,140
Looks to me like
he's getting kind of sleepy.

34
00:07:13,430 --> 00:07:15,890
I think it's time we all left.

35
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:17,690
Come on.

36
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:37,830
Thumper. Come on.

37
00:07:40,750 --> 00:07:42,840
Whatcha gonna call him?

38
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:47,760
Well, I think I'll call him Bambi.

39
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:54,760
Yep, I guess that'll do all right.

40
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,640
Bambi.

41
00:07:57,690 --> 00:07:59,690
My little Bambi.

42
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:33,220
Walking already.
Well, what do you know.

43
00:08:49,450 --> 00:08:52,410
-Good morning.
-Good morning, Mrs Quail.

44
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:55,080
And where's the young prince this...

45
00:08:57,870 --> 00:09:01,290
-Good morning, Bambi.
-Good morning, young prince.

46
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:05,880
Goodbye.

47
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:11,720
Good morning, young prince.

48
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:20,140
Good morning, young prince.

49
00:09:34,570 --> 00:09:36,030
Good morning.

50
00:09:37,740 --> 00:09:39,330
Nice sunny day.

51
00:09:51,630 --> 00:09:53,720
-What's the matter?
-What happened?

52
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:56,760
Did the young prince fall down?

53
00:09:56,850 --> 00:10:00,260
-Is he hurt?
-No, he's all right.

54
00:10:02,140 --> 00:10:04,770
He doesn't walk very good, does he?

55
00:10:04,850 --> 00:10:06,730
Thumper.

56
00:10:07,820 --> 00:10:09,150
Yes, Mama?

57
00:10:10,490 --> 00:10:12,530
What did your father tell you
this morning?

58
00:10:16,450 --> 00:10:19,530
If you can't say something nice,

59
00:10:22,830 --> 00:10:25,830
don't say nothing at all.

60
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:30,130
Come on, Bambi, get up. Try again.

61
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:34,260
Come on, get up. Get up.

62
00:10:34,340 --> 00:10:46,310
-Get up.
-Try again.

63
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:13,550
I'm thumping.
That's why they call me Thumper.

64
00:11:14,590 --> 00:11:16,590
Thumper!

65
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:37,530
Come on. You can do it.

66
00:11:38,410 --> 00:11:41,370
Hop over it. Like this.

67
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:45,870
Hop over it.

68
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,420
Like this.

69
00:12:02,470 --> 00:12:04,930
You didn't hop far enough.

70
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:10,850
That's it. Now the other one.

71
00:12:21,410 --> 00:12:24,620
Gee whiz, what happened that time?

72
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:44,470
Those are birds.

73
00:12:49,690 --> 00:12:51,940
Look, he's trying to talk.

74
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:56,360
He's trying to say "bird."

75
00:12:58,740 --> 00:13:00,740
Say "bird."

76
00:13:04,410 --> 00:13:06,200
Bird.

77
00:13:10,710 --> 00:13:12,620
Bird.

78
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:15,090
Come on, say "bird," say "bird."

79
00:13:15,170 --> 00:13:18,170
Say "bird." Say "bird."
Come on, say "bird."

80
00:13:18,260 --> 00:13:20,260
Say "bird."

81
00:13:22,380 --> 00:13:23,840
Bird.

82
00:13:26,010 --> 00:13:29,060
He talked. He talked, Mama.

83
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:31,560
The young prince said "bird."

84
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:34,520
Bird, bird, bird...

85
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,290
Bird.

86
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:57,590
No, that's not a bird.

87
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:59,920
That's a butterfly.

88
00:14:00,010 --> 00:14:02,130
Butterfly?

89
00:14:02,220 --> 00:14:03,590
Butter...

90
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:09,810
Butterfly.

91
00:14:09,890 --> 00:14:11,850
No, that's a flower.

92
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:16,270
-Flower?
-It's pretty.

93
00:14:21,690 --> 00:14:23,030
Pretty.

94
00:14:30,750 --> 00:14:32,580
Flower.

95
00:14:32,660 --> 00:14:34,160
Me?

96
00:14:39,130 --> 00:14:41,380
No, no, no, no.

97
00:14:42,670 --> 00:14:45,260
That's not a flower.

98
00:14:45,340 --> 00:14:48,010
-He's a little...
-That's all right.

99
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:52,890
He can call me a flower if he wants to.

100
00:14:57,150 --> 00:14:59,610
I don't mind.

101
00:15:03,530 --> 00:15:06,030
Pretty. Pretty flower.

102
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:13,100
Gosh.

103
00:15:25,550 --> 00:15:29,010
I think I better go home now.

104
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:27,900
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

105
00:16:27,990 --> 00:16:30,150
Beating a tune
As you fall all around

106
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:33,280
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

107
00:16:33,370 --> 00:16:35,950
What can compare
With your beautiful sound?

108
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:38,790
Beautiful sound
Beautiful sound

109
00:16:38,870 --> 00:16:41,170
Drip, drop
Drip, drop

110
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:43,790
Drip, drip, drop
When the sky is cloudy

111
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:46,000
Your pretty music
Can brighten the day

112
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:49,010
Drip, drip, drop
When the sky is cloudy

113
00:16:49,090 --> 00:16:51,720
You come along
with a song right away

114
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:53,680
Come with your beautiful music

115
00:16:53,930 --> 00:16:56,350
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

116
00:16:56,430 --> 00:16:59,060
Beating a tune
As you fall all around

117
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:01,690
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

118
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:04,190
What can compare
With your beautiful sound?

119
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,940
Drip, drip, drop
When the sky is cloudy

120
00:17:07,030 --> 00:17:09,780
You come along
With your pretty little song

121
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:12,070
Drip, drip, drop
When the sky is cloudy

122
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:14,530
You come along
With your pretty little song

123
00:17:14,620 --> 00:17:17,160
-Gay little roundelay
-Gay little roundelay

124
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:19,750
-Song of the rainy day
-Song of the rainy day

125
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:22,330
How I love to hear your patter
Pretty little pitter-patter

126
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:25,040
Helter skelter, when you pelter
Troubles always seem to scatter

127
00:17:25,130 --> 00:17:27,500
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

128
00:17:27,590 --> 00:17:30,340
Beating a sound as you fall all around

129
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:32,680
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

130
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:35,640
-Little April shower
-With your beautiful sound

131
00:19:08,020 --> 00:19:10,820
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

132
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:13,440
Beating a tune
As you fall all around

133
00:19:13,530 --> 00:19:16,110
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

134
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:18,780
What can compare
With your beautiful sound?

135
00:19:18,870 --> 00:19:21,910
Beautiful sound

136
00:19:53,900 --> 00:19:56,740
Mother, what we going to do today?

137
00:19:56,820 --> 00:19:59,400
I'm going to take you to the meadow.

138
00:19:59,870 --> 00:20:02,950
Meadow? What's the meadow?

139
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:05,910
It's a very wonderful place.

140
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:08,830
Then why haven't we
been there before?

141
00:20:08,920 --> 00:20:11,540
You weren't big enough.

142
00:20:11,630 --> 00:20:14,340
-Mother, you know what?
-What?

143
00:20:14,420 --> 00:20:17,510
We're not the only deer in the forest.

144
00:20:17,590 --> 00:20:20,970
-Where did you hear that?
-Thumper told me.

145
00:20:21,050 --> 00:20:23,010
Well, he's right.

146
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:25,720
There are many deer in the forest
besides us.

147
00:20:25,810 --> 00:20:28,310
Then why don't I ever see them?

148
00:20:28,390 --> 00:20:31,440
-You will, sometime.
-On the meadow?

149
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:33,270
Perhaps.

150
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:34,650
Hush now.

151
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:38,320
We're almost there.

152
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:50,210
-The meadow.
-Wait.

153
00:20:50,620 --> 00:20:52,790
Bambi, wait.

154
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:57,380
You must never rush out
on the meadow.

155
00:20:57,460 --> 00:20:59,460
There might be danger.

156
00:21:00,380 --> 00:21:02,890
Out there, we're unprotected.

157
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:05,430
The meadow is wide and open,

158
00:21:05,510 --> 00:21:08,100
and there are no trees or bushes
to hide us.

159
00:21:08,180 --> 00:21:10,520
So we have to be very careful.

160
00:21:11,850 --> 00:21:13,520
Wait here.

161
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:19,780
I'll go out first.
And if the meadow is safe, I'll call you.

162
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:14,210
Come on, Bambi. It's all right.

163
00:22:18,550 --> 00:22:20,000
Come on.

164
00:23:11,430 --> 00:23:13,560
Good morning, Prince Bambi.

165
00:23:14,140 --> 00:23:16,060
Good morning, young prince.

166
00:23:16,140 --> 00:23:18,860
Hello. What ya eatin'?

167
00:23:18,940 --> 00:23:22,110
-Clover.
-It's awfully good.

168
00:23:22,190 --> 00:23:24,190
It's delicious.

169
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:26,780
Why don't you try some?

170
00:23:29,370 --> 00:23:32,790
No, not that green stuff.

171
00:23:33,290 --> 00:23:35,500
Just eat the blossoms.

172
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:37,580
That's the good stuff.

173
00:23:39,290 --> 00:23:40,330
Thumper.

174
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:45,760
-Yes, Mama?
-What did your father tell you?

175
00:23:46,170 --> 00:23:47,720
About what?

176
00:23:47,800 --> 00:23:51,850
About eating the blossoms
and leaving the greens?

177
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:54,220
Oh, that one.

178
00:23:56,350 --> 00:24:00,060
Eating greens is a special treat.

179
00:24:00,150 --> 00:24:04,360
It makes long ears and great big feet.

180
00:24:05,650 --> 00:24:09,650
But it sure is awful stuff to eat.

181
00:24:10,700 --> 00:24:13,660
I made that last part up myself.

182
00:24:17,330 --> 00:24:20,420
Watch out.

183
00:25:22,690 --> 00:25:25,190
That's little Faline.

184
00:25:26,150 --> 00:25:29,110
He's kind of bashful, isn't he, Mama?

185
00:25:29,190 --> 00:25:32,950
Well, maybe he wouldn't be
if you'd say hello.

186
00:25:36,580 --> 00:25:38,240
Hello, Bambi.

187
00:25:42,370 --> 00:25:44,920
I said hello.

188
00:25:45,880 --> 00:25:47,340
Well, aren't you going to answer her?

189
00:25:50,550 --> 00:25:52,720
You're not afraid, are you?

190
00:25:56,010 --> 00:25:58,100
Well, then, go ahead.

191
00:26:04,270 --> 00:26:06,270
Go on, say hello.

192
00:26:10,400 --> 00:26:22,410
Hello.

193
00:26:49,900 --> 00:28:27,120
You.

194
00:29:27,930 --> 00:29:30,520
He stopped and looked at me.

195
00:29:30,600 --> 00:29:32,640
Yes, I know.

196
00:29:33,190 --> 00:29:37,230
Why was everyone still
when he came on the meadow?

197
00:29:37,320 --> 00:29:39,650
Everyone respects him.

198
00:29:39,740 --> 00:29:45,620
For of all the deer in the forest,
not one has lived half so long.

199
00:29:46,330 --> 00:29:50,120
He's very brave and very wise.

200
00:29:51,290 --> 00:30:17,730
That's why he's known as
the Great Prince of the Forest.

201
00:31:49,700 --> 00:31:53,540
Mother, look.
What's all that white stuff?

202
00:31:54,700 --> 00:31:57,160
Why, it's snow.

203
00:31:57,460 --> 00:31:59,750
-Snow?
-Yes.

204
00:31:59,840 --> 00:32:02,300
Winter has come.

205
00:33:05,690 --> 00:33:07,940
Hiya, Bambi.

206
00:33:08,530 --> 00:33:10,650
Watch what I can do.

207
00:33:26,630 --> 00:33:29,340
Come on. It's all right.

208
00:33:29,420 --> 00:33:30,800
Look.

209
00:33:31,630 --> 00:33:33,640
The water's stiff.

210
00:33:49,650 --> 00:33:52,490
Some fun, huh, Bambi?

211
00:33:55,370 --> 00:34:04,120
Come on, get up. Like this.

212
00:34:17,180 --> 00:34:19,140
No, no, no.

213
00:34:38,620 --> 00:34:41,370
Kinda wobbly, aren't you?

214
00:35:02,560 --> 00:35:06,140
Got to watch both ends
at the same time.

215
00:35:12,070 --> 00:35:30,590
Guess you better unwind it.

216
00:36:09,120 --> 00:36:11,880
Wake up. Wake up, Flower.

217
00:36:15,470 --> 00:36:18,380
Is it spring yet?

218
00:36:18,970 --> 00:36:21,590
No. Winter's just started.

219
00:36:22,300 --> 00:36:24,970
What you doing? Hibernating?

220
00:36:30,900 --> 00:36:33,150
What do you want to do that for?

221
00:36:34,780 --> 00:36:38,650
All us flowers sleep in the winter.

222
00:36:42,320 --> 00:37:09,310
Well, good night.

223
00:37:59,570 --> 00:38:02,150
Let's sing a gay little spring song

224
00:38:03,070 --> 00:38:05,820
This is the season to sing

225
00:38:05,910 --> 00:38:09,660
So I'd like to suggest
That we all do our best

226
00:38:09,750 --> 00:38:12,710
And warble a song about spring

227
00:38:12,790 --> 00:38:15,210
Spring, spring, spring

228
00:38:15,290 --> 00:38:17,500
Let's get together and sing

229
00:38:22,300 --> 00:38:25,050
Let's sing a gay little spring song

230
00:38:25,970 --> 00:38:28,850
Just like the bird on the wing

231
00:38:28,930 --> 00:38:32,480
Things always seem right
When you're cheerful and bright

232
00:38:32,560 --> 00:38:35,230
So let's get together and sing

233
00:38:35,310 --> 00:38:37,900
Sing, sing, sing

234
00:38:37,980 --> 00:38:41,280
Let's sing a song about spring

235
00:38:41,360 --> 00:38:44,780
Let's twitter and tweet
Like the birdies in May

236
00:38:44,860 --> 00:38:48,200
Get into the mood
And be merry today

237
00:38:48,990 --> 00:38:51,100
Forget all your troubles
And warble away...

238
00:38:52,080 --> 00:38:53,200
Wait.

239
00:38:53,830 --> 00:38:55,830
What now?

240
00:38:58,130 --> 00:39:00,090
Hey.

241
00:39:01,210 --> 00:39:02,920
Stop that racket.

242
00:39:03,010 --> 00:39:04,180
Scat.

243
00:39:06,180 --> 00:39:08,800
Let's sing a song about spring

244
00:39:09,850 --> 00:39:11,430
I'll fix 'em.

245
00:39:18,900 --> 00:39:23,440
There. I guess that'll teach 'em.

246
00:39:28,070 --> 00:39:30,660
Oh, what's the use?

247
00:39:33,660 --> 00:39:36,330
This is the season to sing...

248
00:39:40,210 --> 00:39:42,800
Same thing every spring.

249
00:39:50,180 --> 00:39:52,510
Love's sweet song.

250
00:39:54,350 --> 00:39:56,810
Pain in the pin feathers, I call it.

251
00:40:17,500 --> 00:40:18,620
Stop it.

252
00:40:22,210 --> 00:40:24,380
Get out of here. All of you.

253
00:40:27,340 --> 00:40:28,930
And you, too.

254
00:40:30,390 --> 00:40:34,140
Hello, Friend Owl.
Don't you remember me?

255
00:40:34,220 --> 00:40:36,520
Why, it's the young prince.

256
00:40:36,890 --> 00:40:38,270
Bambi!

257
00:40:39,860 --> 00:40:42,480
My, my, how you've changed.

258
00:40:42,570 --> 00:40:45,400
Turn round there. Let me look at you.

259
00:40:45,740 --> 00:40:49,240
I see you've traded in your spots
for a pair of antlers.

260
00:40:53,160 --> 00:40:57,750
You know, just the other day
I was talking to myself about you.

261
00:40:57,830 --> 00:41:00,620
And we were wondering
what had become of you.

262
00:41:00,710 --> 00:41:02,710
Hello, Bambi.

263
00:41:04,170 --> 00:41:05,750
Remember me?

264
00:41:06,970 --> 00:41:08,010
Thumper.

265
00:41:09,180 --> 00:41:10,430
Right.

266
00:41:15,060 --> 00:41:17,060
Hi, fellas.

267
00:41:17,560 --> 00:41:18,850
Flower.

268
00:41:19,770 --> 00:41:21,230
Yeah.

269
00:41:31,950 --> 00:41:34,820
Well, what's the matter with them?

270
00:41:34,910 --> 00:41:37,240
Why are they acting that way?

271
00:41:37,830 --> 00:41:39,100
Why, don't you know?

272
